<p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 39</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>And I will give grass in your field for your cattle. (Deuteronomy 11)</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Grass initials make peace in His heights in your field, language of plundering and breaking when a person feels some hunger, that the desire of eating overcomes him know that he has enemies (see Bava Metzia 59b)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Who sets peace in your border</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Psalms 147) and one who has poor below, it is known that he has poor above (Sanhedrin 103b) therefore one needs to plunder and break his animality that desires to eat for the main of the hunger is to the animality (Bereishit parsha 63) pride comes and disgrace comes, this is the disgrace of hunger, as it is written (Ezekiel 36)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Which you shall no longer bear the disgrace of hunger among the nations</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;it turns out the dispute, that is what they disgrace a person comes through this the aspect of hunger and this hunger, that is the aspect of dispute, the aspect of disgrace, it is the aspect of foreskin as it is written (Genesis 34):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>For it is a disgrace to us</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and the foreskin they are three shells, that surround the&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>bris</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;peace and when they break the foreskin, then the&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>bris</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;peace is revealed and when there is peace below, there is peace above in His heights and when there is peace above, then great satiety is revealed and increased in the world as it is written by Joseph (there 47):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Give seed and we shall live</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;another explanation (Job 5)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And your offspring like the grass of the earth</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;in your field for your cattle that is when will you have living and enduring sons when your mating will be in holiness and you break your desiring soul, that is the animal soul and it shall seem to you as if you force a demon (Nedarim 20b) and this in your field, language of demon through this you will have enduring sons for the death of sons, this is because of the oppressed souls in the balance as known (see Zohar Mishpatim 113a) for the balance, that is shells of nogah, it is close to the animal soul, as brought (in Mishnat Chassidim in tractate of composition). Also one needs that the main of your mating be on Sabbath night that then it is included in holiness, and all workers of iniquity separate from it and this&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And you shall eat and be satisfied</b></span><span class="body-text">, this hints on Sabbath that then the satiety from which the six days are blessed.</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 40</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>These are the journeys of the children of Israel.</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">It is brought in the ten utterances: These are the journeys of the children of Israel because they sinned in these are your gods Israel because of this the children of Israel shall journey it turns out all the journeys of a person, it is because of the spoiling of the faith that is the aspect of idol worship for if he believed in complete faith that the Holy One, blessed be He, can prepare for him all his needs he would not journey any journey it turns out that the journey is spoiling of faith, that is the aspect of idol worship and this that is written in idol worship (Isaiah 30):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Go out say to him</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;go out, this is the aspect of journey and movement. Also through movement he rectifies the movement that he caused as if above (there 28)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the molten image is narrow as it gathers</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;also through idol worship, the rain is withheld as it is written (Deuteronomy 11)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And you shall serve other gods etc. and there shall be no rain</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and when there is no rain, there is no satiety (Psalms 72)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>The mountains shall bear peace for the people</b></span><span class="body-text">, as Rashi explained then no man helps his fellow and each one needs to journey and move from place to place, for his sustenance also the exile comes on the negation of Torah, as it is written (Isaiah 5):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>My people are exiled for lack of knowledge</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and through idol worship, comes withholding of rains and when there is no flour, there is no Torah (Avot chapter 3).</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 41</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Dances</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Dances behold it is brought (in Etz Chayim folio 22a) the knees that is the legs, they are netzach hod, and they are heels and heel gematria two times Elokim, which are judgments, that there is grasping there for the externals as known and the action to drive away the externals from there, that he draws into the knees, the strengths from the root of understanding and when he draws the root of the strengths from understanding, then the externals flee from there, and he takes the birthright and the blessing, that this is the aspect of knees and the root of the birthrights, is called wine as known and this is wine that gladdens and this that is written by Jacob, when he saw that he is the aspect of knees in the place of judgment for two times Elokim with ten letters gematria Jacob then he drew the root of the strengths, the aspect of wine that gladdens as it is written (Genesis 27):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And he brought him wine and he drank</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;the root of the blessing it turns out through dances, that drinks wine that gladdens, which are the root of the strengths that are in the understanding and are drawn below into the legs, that is that he dances in this drives away the externals from there and this is the flaming of the dance, and it is&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A fire offering a pleasing aroma to Hashem</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Numbers 28) but one who dances in flaming of the inclination this is called the sin of Nadav and Avihu that it is written by them (Leviticus 10): And they offered strange fire Nadav and Avihu, they are netzach and hod and flaming that is in holiness, is called wine that gladdens, that through it the birthrights are sweetened and strange fire, is called wine that intoxicates, flaming of the inclination and there is Heaven forbid grasping for the externals, which He did not command them and this also is redemption of soul for the money is called pillars, as it is written (Deuteronomy 11):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the standing that is on their feet</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Pesachim 119a) and when the&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadik</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;who does the redemption lays his hands on the money he should intend for there is the great hand etc., and that is three hands and three times yud gematria 42 and the name of 42 has seven names and each name has six letters and he should intend to draw to him the vavs, that is the seven names that each one has six letters to draw them into the money which is called pillars and then it is called vavs of the pillars and these pillars, that is legs that is heels, they are the aspect of judgment for two times Elokim, gematria heel and there is grasping there for the externals and judgment is not sweetened except in its root and the root of the judgments in the understanding, as it is written (in the Zohar Vayikra 10a): Understanding judgments are aroused from it,&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>I am understanding power is mine</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Proverbs 8) and the name of 42 in the understanding it turns out when he draws the name of 42 into pillars then the judgments are sweetened in their root (Exodus 27):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Vavs of the pillars and their fillets silver</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;explanation: through attachment and connection vavs with pillars, there is made silver, kindness, that the judgments are sweetened Etz Chayim chapter 13 (hall of the crowns gate 1): Name of 42 in the understanding, and these 42 they are 300 lights that illuminate 8 whiteness gematria in peace (there in chapter 14) gematria chashmal garment, that this chashmal guards upper garments from the moth of shell, as it is written (Isaiah 51):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Like a garment the moth shall eat them</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and this (Yoma 71b): One who wants to pour wine on the altar, let him fill the throats of Torah scholars to pour, that is kingship and dominion (Psalms 2):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I have poured My king</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;etc. Wine, this is the aspect of understanding, root of the birthright wine that gladdens altar this is the aspect of judgments Torah scholars, they are the aspect of netzach hod and this is its explanation: One who wants to make king and to rule and to sweeten the judgments, through their root which is wine that gladdens what shall he do, good advice: On this let him fill their throats, through dances, or through redemption, as brought above also through filling their throats, the judgments are sweetened (end of Berakhot): Torah scholars increase peace in the world that through them the name of 42 is drawn, which are 300 lights, and with 8 whiteness, gematria in peace and Torah scholars are called netzach hod, legs as brought in the Midrash:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>His legs pillars of marble</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;they are Torah scholars (see Targum) and also altar is called legs, as it is written (Psalms 4):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Sacrifice sacrifices of righteousness</b></span><span class="body-text">, and as it is written (there 85):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Righteousness shall go before Him</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and this is the explanation (there 20)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>May He give you according to your heart</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and when, when&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And all your counsel He will fulfill</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;through filling the throats of Torah scholars (Avot chapter 6): And they enjoy from him counsel and wisdom and as it is written (there 33):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>The counsel of Hashem stands forever</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;that they are pillars of the world (Isaiah 14)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Hashem of hosts has counseled</b></span><span class="body-text">, Hashem of hosts, they are netzach and hod.</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 42</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>And He saw their distress when He heard their cry etc. (Psalms 106)</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Behold through music, the judgments are sweetened as it is written in the holy Zohar (Pinchas 215a) the bow it is the Shechinah and three colors of the bow, they are the fathers, and they are garments of the Shechinah and when it is clothed in garments of lights then&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant</b></span><span class="body-text">, then and the wrath of the king subsided parable to a king who was angry at his son and when the king sees the queen in garments of lights then he has mercy on his son and letters of the prayer it is the Shechinah, as it is written (Psalms 51):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Adonai open my lips</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;that the speech is the name Adonai and is called bow as Rashi explained (Genesis 48):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>With my sword and with my bow</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;language of prayer and the voice of the music they are three colors of the bow that there are in the voice fire, water, wind, which are three fathers that the fathers they are three colors of lights, in which&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;etc. it turns out one who plays the letters of the prayer and the voice of the music they are in merit and in great brightness then he clothes the Shechinah, that is the letters, in garments of lights and the Holy One blessed be He sees it, then and the wrath of the king subsided and this that Rashi explained&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>When He heard their cry</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;in the merit of the fathers that is when the music, which are three colors of the bow as above, in brightness and in great merit for the three colors they are the fathers as above and they are garments of the Shechinah and when the garments are lights in merit and in brightness, is called merit of the fathers then:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant</b></span><span class="body-text">, then:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And He relented according to the abundance of His kindness</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;that is: And the wrath of the king subsided, and the judgments are sweetened also through faith in sages that he believes that all their words and their deeds are not simple, and there are secrets in them through this he clothes the bow in garments of lights then:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;for the&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadik</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;is the aspect of bow as Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai said to Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi: Was a bow seen in your days etc. (Ketubot 77b) and it is brought in the holy Zohar (parsha Pinchas folio 215a): One whose deeds to illuminate in them the Matronita and to strip from her garments of darkness that she stripped and to adorn her in garments of colors of secrets of the Torah what is written in it?&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;that light secret is called and in that time anger rises from him and the wrath of the king subsided also one who makes a fine garment for the&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadik</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;through this the judgments are sweetened also this is aspects of blowings for blowing shevarim teruah, they are the fathers Abraham Isaac Jacob and your sign bow that is blowing etc. (Zohar parsha Pinchas 230a) and this is (Job 22):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the Almighty shall be in your distress</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;for the name Almighty they are the fathers (there 231a) for sh three branches of the tree, which are the fathers and they are three names of the unity, Hashem our G-d Hashem which are 14 letters, and they are 14 of Almighty Abraham Isaac Jacob, they are the initials of Hashem our G-d Hashem&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>There is no saying and there are no words without their voice being heard</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Psalms 19) this is the aspect of bow and voice, three colors of the bow.</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 43</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>The speeches of the wicked produce licentiousness in the hearer</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Know that the speeches of the wicked who is a man of knowledge, produce&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>licentiousness</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;in the hearer for the matings are drawn from the knowledge as it is written (Genesis 4):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the man knew Eve his wife</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and it is written (Numbers 31)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Every woman who has known a man</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;but there are two kinds of matings that is mating of holiness, it is attachment to&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadikim</i></span><span class="body-text">, and to the Torah, and to Hashem, blessed be He, this is drawn from knowledge of holiness and matings of transgression, are drawn from knowledge of shell and the speech is the revelation of the knowledge for they do not know what is in the knowledge, except through the speech as it is written (Psalms 19)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And night to night declares knowledge</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;declares from language of speech that the speech speaks what is in the knowledge and when a wicked speaks and brings out from his mouth vanities produces poisonous airs of&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>licentiousness</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and the hearer from him the speeches, and breathes breaths inserts into his body these airs and therefore by Balaam who is aspects of knowledge of shell as our sages expounded, of blessed memory (Sifri parsha And this is the blessing, and in the Zohar Exodus 21b, Balak 193b): On the verse no one has arisen like Moses etc. in Israel no one has arisen, but in the nations has arisen, and who Balaam (Vayikra Rabbah 9) and therefore when Moab took counsel from Midian, they said to them: His power is only in the mouth for the mouth is the revelation of the knowledge Moab said also we will come upon them with a man whose power is in the mouth (as brought in Rashi in parsha Balak) for he also is knowledge of shell, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 7):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>This opposite this G-d made</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Numbers 24):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And knows the knowledge of the Most High</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and our rabbis expounded of blessed memory (Berakhot 7a): That he knew when the Holy One blessed be He is angry for when the knowledge is not in settlement, then there is anger as our rabbis said, of blessed memory (Pesachim 66b): Anyone who is angry his wisdom departs from him and therefore when Moses our master, peace be upon him, was angry at the officers of the army when they came from Midian the knowledge departed from him and Eleazar needed to say the laws of immersion of vessels and when the knowledge is complete, then there is no anger, as it is written (Isaiah 11):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>They shall not hurt nor destroy in all My holy mountain for the earth shall be full of knowledge</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and Balaam was looking in knowledge of shell, which is the excesses of upper knowledge and when it changes he knew that the Holy One blessed be He is in anger it turns out that Balaam is knowledge of shell and through his speeches he produced poisonous airs of&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>licentiousness</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;to this when they came from the war of Midian, it is written (Numbers 31):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And Moses was angry with the officers of the army, and he said have you kept every female alive, behold they were through the word of Balaam</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;through the word precisely, for through his words, which is the revelation of his knowledge, he produced&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>licentiousness</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;in Midian and therefore when they came from the wars of Midian, it is written (there):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the heads of the officers approached Moses etc. and they said and we have brought near the offering of Hashem etc., to atone for our souls before Hashem</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and our rabbis expounded, of blessed memory (Shabbat 64a): That thus they said even though from the hands of transgression we came out, from the hands of thought we did not come out.</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 44</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>What one strikes palm to palm at the time of prayer</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">What one strikes palm to palm at the time of prayer for our sages said, of blessed memory (Bereishit Rabbah parsha 1): Why did the Torah begin from Bereishit for the nations will say to us robbers you are, that you conquered the land of seven nations because of this, the power of His works He declared to His people that He declared that all the worlds all are the works of His hands and to whom the Holy One blessed be He wants He gives and this, to give them the inheritance of nations, for in His hand all and all the things are called the power of His works opposite 28 letters of the work of Bereishit, opposite 28 joints of the hands and this is known that the air of the land of the nations it is impure (see Shabbat 15b Gittin 8a Nazir 54a 55b) and the air of the land of Israel it is holy and pure for the Holy One blessed be He took out from under the hand of the nations and gave to us but the land of peoples, which is outside the land, there air impure and when we clap palm to palm, in this 28 letters of the work of Bereishit are aroused, the power of His works and it turns out that in His hand to give us the inheritance of nations for all is of the Holy One blessed be He and in this there is power in our hand to purify the air of the land of the peoples for the land of the peoples returns under the dominion of the Holy One blessed be He and in His hand to give to whomever He wants, as it is written:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>To give them the inheritance of nations</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and then the air of the place where the Israelite man prays is purified and he draws holy air like in the land of Israel. Also through clapping of palm, the impure air is driven away for through [clapping of] palms a voice is heard and this voice it is holy air from 28 letters of the work of Bereishit, from 28 joints of the hands as we see in sense, that the air is driven away through clapping of palms and because of this one needs to fix a place for his prayer (Berakhot 6b) as we see in sense, that people who come to a province that they are not accustomed to its air through this they weaken and die even from an evil abode to a beautiful abode (see Ketubot 110b) so the matter in prayer even when he stands to pray in a place where a&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadik</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;prayed nevertheless it is very hard for him to pray there for he is not accustomed to the air of the place all the more from a beautiful abode to an evil abode and this that our sages said, of blessed memory (there): Anyone who fixes a place etc., the G-d of Abraham in his help for through him the world is built anew and building of the world through Abraham, as it is written (Psalms 89)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A world of kindness shall be built</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and this that is brought in the Tikkunim Tikkun 22 (folio 66a) and with this power Israel are strengthened over Edom. And further, (there): One needs to raise this power to the side of wisdom and this is the aspect of: Anyone who fixes a place for his prayer the G-d of Abraham in his help for Abraham he is right, one who wants to become wise let him go south (Bava Batra 25b) and further, the G-d of Abraham in his help for Abraham he is first to the attainment of the land of Israel as it is brought in the Zohar (Lech Lecha 78b) stumble in the balance until it is revealed to him and this is the explanation, (Berakhot 26b): Prayers opposite the continual offerings they instituted continual, this is aspects of the land of Israel (see Shocher Tov Psalm 105 Deuteronomy 11) as it is written&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Continually the eyes of Hashem your G-d are upon it</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;that is one needs to see that he pray his prayer in the air of the land of Israel that is the rectification of foreign thoughts that are in the prayer which they are aspects of prayers opposite as above their rectification through continual, through aspects of the land of Israel and this is the explanation, (Hosea 12):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And by the hand of the prophets I will be likened</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;through the hands, through clapping of palm, the speeches are spoken in the land of holiness (Zechariah 2 Rashi Exodus 6 on And Aaron your brother shall be your prophet). Also through clapping of palm, killing and destruction are nullified from the world for the hands they are aspects of:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Let there be light and there was light</b></span><span class="body-text">, right and left and it is written (Genesis 1):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And G-d saw the light etc., and He separated between the light</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;this is Aaron (Tikkunim Tikkun 30 71b) and this is aspects of (Leviticus 26):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will give peace in the land and a sword shall not pass through your land</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>You stand this day</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(Deuteronomy 29): There is no standing but prayer (Berakhot 6b)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Before Hashem your G-d</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;this is aspects of the land of Israel as our sages said of blessed memory (Ketubot 110b): Anyone who dwells in the land of Israel is like one who has a G-d that is through what will you merit that your prayer be in the air of the land of Israel your heads your tribes etc., and counts ten aspects, that is aspects of clapping of palm through clapping of palms, the prayer is in the air of the land of Israel as above. Prayers opposite continual offerings etc., that is aspects of the land of Israel that is through clapping of palm, foreign thoughts are nullified for anyone who dwells outside the land is like one who has no G-d and anyone who dwells in the land of Israel is like one who has a G-d and through clapping of palm then he dwells in the air of the land of Israel and he has a G-d and foreign thoughts are nullified (Exodus 17)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And his hands were faith until the sun came</b></span><span class="body-text">, and its Targum: Spread in prayer and opposite faith, they are the denials foreign thoughts of nations and their rectification through continual offerings, through the land of Israel, through clapping of palm and this is the explanation, (Isaiah 62):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And you shall be a crown of splendor in the hand of Hashem</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;explanation: Through the hand of Hashem, through clapping of palm that the hands of the Holy One blessed be He are aroused as above through this the thoughts of nations are rectified for through nations he damages in splendor, as it is written (there 44):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>As the splendor of a man to dwell in the house</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;when he rectifies his thoughts through this there is made a crown of splendor that splendor is crowned with the crown that his mother crowned him (Song of Songs 3) another explanation prayers opposite that is the foreign thoughts which are opposite which confuse his prayer and are called flood which confuse his prayer and their rectification that he give charity to the land of Israel and through this he is included in the land of Israel upon which it is said:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A land that is not rained upon on the day of wrath</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;(as our rabbis expounded of blessed memory Zevachim 113a) and through this he is saved from foreign thoughts and this continual offerings their institution, their rectification through the land of Israel upon which it is said:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>A land which etc. continually the eyes of Hashem your G-d are upon it</b></span><span class="body-text">. Also the air of the land of Israel makes wise (Bava Batra 158b) and through this the brain is purified, that is his thought (Genesis 9)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and I will see it, through aspects of the land of Israel through this the everlasting&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>bris</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;is aroused and rectified aspects of prayer, 18 blessings of prayer,&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadik</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;lives of worlds [all this matter from the beginning of sign 44 until here is connected together. And so we heard many these things in one exposition. But in his holy writing, he divided them a little and so was his way several times, and I did not know his reason].</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 45</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Clapping of palms in prayer</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Clapping of palms at the time of prayer this is aspects of giving the bed between north to south (Berakhot 5b) for bed that is aspects of mating aspects of prayer (Tikkun 10 and see Tikkun 58) and north and south, this is aspects of hands and this that Abba Binyamin prayed (Berakhot 5b): That his prayer be close to his bed that is that there be no separation between the prayer to the mating also through clapping of palm, the judgments are sweetened for there are three havayot, which are the aspect of three hands the great hand the strong hand, the high hand and the right hand this is the great hand and the left hand, this is the strong hand and at the time of striking that they are connected together this is the aspect of high hand and the speeches that come out, they come out from the throat gematria three times Elokim and they are sweetened through three havayot and this is the explanation (Psalms 119)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>My soul in my palm continually</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;etc. My soul, this is aspects of speech (Song of Songs 5)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>My soul went out when he spoke</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;in my palm continually, that is when he strikes palm to palm at the time of the prayer through this,&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And Your Torah I have not forgotten</b></span><span class="body-text">, initials shalav gematria three havayot and three Elokim, that is the sweetening of the judgments. Also, the main forgetfulness is from brains of smallness, from aspects of Elokim and when he sweetens the judgments as above, then he is in brains of greatness, and he has no forgetfulness and Your Torah I have not forgotten, initials shalav that is through that he sweetens three Elokim, in three havayot as above, he has no forgetfulness and this precisely at the time of the prayer for then he knows if he is in brains of smallness, or of greatness for the speech is the revelation of the brains as it is written (Proverbs 2):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>From His mouth knowledge and understanding</b></span><span class="body-text">.</span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Likutay Moharan Volume 1: Torah 46</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text"><b>Clapping of palm at the time of prayer</b></span></p><p><span class="body-text">[In the language of our master, of blessed memory]</span></p><p><span class="body-text">Clapping of palm at the time of the prayer this is aspects of arousal of wings, from which the speech comes (Ecclesiastes 10):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the owner of wings shall tell the matter</b></span><span class="body-text">, and it is written (Ezekiel 10)&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And hands of a man from under their wings</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;it turns out that through that a person arouses in his hands, then [the wings] are aroused that is wings of the lung, from which the speech is formed but still they need to prepare and rectify mouth, to receive the speech within it and through that he strikes palm to palm through this the mouth is formed for in each hand five fingers and the strikings the lights, right hand in left hand that is five times five gematria twenty-five and the strikings left hand in right hand five times five gematria also twenty-five two times twenty-five gematria fifty this is aspects of fifty times the exodus from Egypt that is mentioned in the Torah for through aspects of jubilee they went out from the exile of Egypt (Zohar Exodus 46a) and the main exile of Egypt, that the speech was in exile and because of this Moses was heavy of mouth and through redemption the aspect of mouth was formed it turns out that through fifty gates of understanding the mouth was formed and this is (Exodus 4):&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Who placed a mouth in man</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;who precisely it turns out that through clapping of palm five fingers right in the five that are in left hand and five that are in left hand in the five that are in right hand the aspect of who is formed through which the mouth was formed, as it is written&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>Who placed a mouth in man</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and the mouth receives the speeches from the wings of the lung, as it is written:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And the owner of wings shall tell the matter</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and wings are aroused in the arousal of the hands of man as it is written:&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And hands of a man from under their wings</b></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;and all this we see in sense, that the hands they are opposite the wings of the lung and because of this the poskim said if the wing broke close to the body invalid (Yoreh Deah sign 53) for certainly the lung was punctured through this.</span></p><p><br/><br/></p> 
